Third-party components

The BSD 3-Clause license above covers scijit's own code: the bind(c) wrappers,
the ctypes/@njit glue, and the pure-@njit ports. scijit also bundles and builds
several established numerical libraries, each under its own license, retained in
src/<pack>/ and summarized in docs/CREDITS.md:

  FITPACK (Dierckx, public domain)        src/fitpack/README
  MINPACK (Argonne; MIT + U. of Chicago)  src/minpack/LICENSE.txt,
                                          src/minpack/LICENSE_NumbaMinpack.txt
  L-BFGS-B (BSD-3)                         src/lbfgsb/LICENSE.txt
  SLSQP (BSD-3)                            src/slsqp/LICENSE
  PRIMA (BSD-3)                            src/prima/LICENCE.txt
  FFTPACK (public domain)                 src/fftpack/LICENSE
  QUADPACK                                src/quadpack/LICENSE
  ODEPACK / LSODA (public domain)         src/odepack/LICENSE
  ARPACK (BSD-3)                           src/arpack/LICENSE_arpack-ng.txt
  Reference LAPACK / BLAS (BSD-3)          src/lapack/LICENSE_lapack.txt
  PROPACK (BSD-3)                          src/propack/LICENSE_propack.txt
  CDFLIB (MIT)                             src/cdflib/LICENSE_cdflib.txt
  AMOS (Sandia / ACM TOMS)                 src/amos/LICENSE_amos.txt

Each bundled component remains under the license shipped alongside it.
The FITPACK sources are public domain and carry no license file.
src/fitpack/README records their provenance and the local
modifications to twelve sources.
